				140,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Air): Apply code formatting and refactor TLS configuration logic\n\nThis commit standardizes code style and refactors internal logic within the Air daemon, focusing on the Downloader and Mountain client modules.\n\n**Style & Imports**\n- Ran `rustfmt` equivalent formatting across `Source/Downloader`, `Source/Library`, and `Source/Mountain`.\n- Consolidated `std` and external imports for improved readability.\n- Removed trailing whitespace and standardized type annotation spacing (e.g., `ident:Type`).\n\n**Air/Mountain (TLS & Connection)**\n- Refactored `create_tls_client_config` to use a `match` statement for branching between mTLS and server-only authentication, replacing previous conditional bindings with a cleaner builder pattern.\n- Simplified `MountainClient::connect` by adopting the standard `tonic::transport::ClientTlsConfig` builder flow, adding TCP keep-alive support, and streamlining how TLS is applied to the gRPC endpoint.\n\nThese changes improve code maintainability and alignment with Rust best practices within the Land ecosystem.",
			"SHA": "846c4af3ffb276443ecace264cfe474ec477662b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-08T21:10:49Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				140,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Air): Implement Mountain client, mTLS, and downloader throttling\n\nThis commit significantly expands the Air daemon's capabilities by introducing a secure gRPC client for communicating with Mountain and refining the resource management of the downloader service.\n\n**Air/Mountain (New Module)**\n- Introduced a new `Mountain` module to establish Air as a gRPC client to the Mountain backend.\n- Implemented `MountainClient` with support for connection management, health checks, and configuration queries.\n- Added comprehensive mTLS (mutual TLS) support using `rustls`. The implementation handles CA certificates, client certificates, and system-native roots, configurable via environment variables or `TlsConfig`.\n- Added `mtls` feature flag to `Cargo.toml` to gate TLS dependencies (`rustls`, `rustls-pemfile`, `tokio-rustls`).\n\n**Air/Downloader (Throttling & IO)**\n- Refactored bandwidth limiting from a simple semaphore to a precise `TokenBucket` algorithm. This allows for accurate rate limiting (bytes/sec) with configurable burst capacity, replacing the previous coarse-grained permit system.\n- Implemented actual disk space checking logic:\n  - Unix: Uses `libc::statvfs` to query available blocks.\n  - Windows: Uses `Win32::Storage::FileSystem::GetDiskFreeSpaceExW`.\n- Updated platform-specific dependencies (`windows` crate, `libc`) in `Cargo.toml` to support these system calls.\n\nThese changes prepare Air for secure inter-service communication within the Land ecosystem and ensure robust, non-intrusive background operations.",
			"SHA": "f9e613f4028b76305babbdb688c51959b29158a8"
		}
	],
